      ],
      "source": "https://shinglehouseborough.org/history",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Moravian missionary David Zeisberger was the first white man to set foot in what is now Shinglehouse in 1767.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://shinglehouseborough.org/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Early settlers noted a circular earth embankment at Assembly Park, once a fortification, though no trace remains today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
